{"id":"00000001794701106578:c752fdea782a03c717f91c806b839160","text":"Source research selected 80 distinct navigation-related commits reachable origin/main from 264 non-merge routing-surface commits since 2026. Reviewed commit intent, changed logic and existing assertion sources. RAN: read-only git/source analysis, no runtime tests, builds or benchmarks. INFERRED: a portable controller protocol should separate One URL/policy from generational screen transactions and accepted/content/presentation milestones. Observation: fff5979cc9 documents external-store sync-lane pathname publication racing the navigator's transition; current router.ts preserves reducer-based publication. The draft's unconditional useSyncExternalStore design has been removed. The regression contract maps historical fixes to existing fixtures and explicit gaps. Searches found no direct useBlocker/usePreventRemove/beforeRemove test in One test sources. protected.test.ios.ts covers auth, not interactive pop. tests/test-warm-routes checks Vite dependency cache reuse/pruning, not state restoration. Existing skipped stress/cross-mode tests are not proof. These findings change migration priorities without claiming replacement correctness."}

